  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">African Food System Transformation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The African Food Systems Transformation (AFST) cluster operates in Africa and follows a business-led approach to contribute to the Better Jobs, Better Incomes, Gender Equality, and Better Environment impact themes. The BU aligns with IDH&apos;s Africa Food Systems Transformation Strategy with the following vision:Transform food value chains into economically viable, inclusive, and resilient ones that contribute to improved food and nutrition security; create local economic value and support increased regional trade in Africa.By &#x201c;inclusive&#x201d;, we refer to the inclusion of smallholder farmers, SMEs, and other disadvantaged and excluded groups (e.g., women and youth) in formal value chains.By &#x201c;resilient value chains&#x201d;, we refer to adopting climate-adaptive and regenerative production practices, and value chain players and practices that support these practices.By &#x201c;creating local economic value,&#x201d; we are increasing value addition and processing in Africa, increasing incomes, and creating employment for youth and women.</narrative>
  </description>
